#
# hatari.mk - the Hatari and zlib sources BMAtariST builds.
#
# These come unmodified from the third_party/hatari submodule. The list
# matches what Hatari's own build (src/CMakeLists.txt and those of src/cpu,
# src/falcon and src/debug) compiles for its libretro core, with zlib and the
# Falcon's DSP, minus the front ends: src/sdl/ and src/gui-sdl/ (SDL) and
# src/retro/ (libretro). BMAtariST's front end is in src/port/ instead
# (HATARI_PORT_SRCS, the same functions as src/retro/ has). scandir.c is
# left out: it needs dirent's d_reclen, which newlib doesn't have, and its
# functions are posix_extra.c's on the Pi.
#
# The CPU core's tables and opcode handlers are generated by two programs
# built for the computer doing the build, build68k and gencpu, as Hatari's
# build does (HATARI_CPUGEN_SRCS; see the Makefile).
#
# When updating Hatari, check its CMakeLists.txt files for added or removed
# files (see docs/UPDATING.md).
#

